  "id": "endogenous-attention",
  "term": "endogenous attention",
  "definition": "Endogenous attention is voluntary, sustained, goal-directed attention that people intentionally direct according to their current aims. It is a top-down process that selects goal-relevant information for further processing, often requiring effort, such as deliberately focusing on a particular location.",
